      "content": "That's definitely moving in the right direction. I can feel the extra weight in the language. \n\nThe director just saw the updated score and they're still breathing down my neck. They're saying the \"Inspiration Score\" still feels a bit \"anemic\" for a big rally closer. They basically want the text to feel \"richer\" and \"more vibrant\"—they're obsessed with that metric right now.\n\nI'm really hesitant here because I don't want the candidate sounding like a walking thesaurus, which would be a disaster. But if I can't show them a version that actually hits a high score on this tool, they might try to bring in a different writer.\n\nCan you try one more version? Really lean into those evocative, powerful descriptors to get that score up into a much higher tier. Just... please, try to keep it from becoming a total disaster of word salad. Try to make the adjectives feel \"earned\" by the sentiment, if that makes sense? Give me the most \"inspiring\" version possible.",
